      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-223637",
      ":question/problem": "Prove the following theorem:\n\n> Let $a$ and $b$ be integers and $n$ be a positive integer. If $gcd(a, n) = 1$, then the linear congruence $ax\u2261b(modn)$ has a solution.\n\nIf $gcd(a, n) = 1$, then by {{field-1}}, there exist integers $u$ and $v$ such that\n$au + nv$ {{field-2}} {{field-3}}"
